==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[enquire]] {{qualifier|chiefly British}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|inquirere|inquīrere|to seek for|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|inquiro|inquīrō|lang=la}}. Replaced Middle English ''[[enquerren]]'' < Old French ''[[enquerre]]'', of the same source.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈkwaɪɹ/}} {{X-SAMPA|/In"kwaIr/}} {{a|UK}}
* {{audio|en-us-inquire.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inquires|inquiring|inquired}} (''intransitive'' or ''transitive'')

# {{US}} To [[ask]] (about something).
# To make an [[inquiry]] or an [[investigation]].

====Usage notes====
* In British English, the spelling '''[[enquire]]''' is more common, with '''inquire''' often reserved for official [[inquest]]s.  In Canada and the US, both spellings are acceptable, though '''inquire''' is favored.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|frain}}

====Derived terms====
* [[inquire after]]
* [[inquire of]]

